.TH "SOPLOS-GAMING-PANEL" "1" "2026-11-18" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-gaming-panel \- live gaming companion for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-gaming-panel
[\fB\-\-toggle\fR | \fB\-\-show\fR | \fB\-\-hud\-toggle\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Soplos Gaming Panel
is the visual surface of the machine while a game runs. It controls
GameMode over D\-Bus, reads and writes the configuration of MangoHud,
watches the use of the processor, the graphics card, the memory and the
temperatures, and opens the games of Steam, Lutris and Heroic that are
already installed.
.PP
The tools it controls are the ones that Soplos Welcome installs in its
Gaming Center; the panel does not install them again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-toggle
Shows the panel if it is hidden and hides it if it is shown. This is what
the shortcut of the desktop runs.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Shows the panel. It is what a second launch does when nothing else is asked.
.TP
.B \-\-hud\-toggle
Turns the small overlay over the game on or off.
.TP
.B \-\-run\-ops \fIFILE\fR
Internal: runs as root the operations of \fIFILE\fR. Only pkexec starts the
program this way, and it never opens a window.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Internal: keeps the governor of the games running with no window. Only the
systemd unit starts the program this way.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon\-restore
Internal: gives the machine back its own settings after the daemon stops.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soplos-gaming-panel/config.json
The choices of the user: language, theme, shortcuts and what the overlay
shows.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/soplos-gaming-panel.desktop
Present while the panel starts with the session.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/soplos-gaming-panel
The requests of the administrator step.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soplos-gaming-panel/covers
The covers the user chooses for the games of the library.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soplos-gaming-panel/mangohud\-fps.csv
The log the panel reads the frames per second from, written by MangoHud when
the panel asks it to.
.TP
.I /var/lib/soplos-gaming-panel/backup
The copies of the files an administrator step touches, taken before it
writes them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gamemoderun (1),
.BR mangohud (1)
